<!--BlockML Documentation — import A03 data into A04
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a04_rendering.task.A04_01_CopyData-->
<task:A04_01_CopyData xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:task="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a04_rendering.task"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <baseType>
    workflow:InstructionTask
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A task that imports A03 data into A04
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A04 rendering task: wipe a04_rendering.data, copy the full
    a03_authoring.data tree into it, then remap packages and names
    so the imported Blocks live only in A04.

    - **Wipe** — delete the live A04 data package before the copy.
      Leftover ignored trees (for example data_IGNORE) are not input
    - **Copy** — the whole A03 data package, not individual DocSet /
      Page / PageGroup sync
    - **Remap** — one pass after the copy: A03 packages and sector
      names become A04; no A04 file may reference another sector
    - **Sources** — this task has no authoritativeSources
  </documentation>
  <properties>
    <instructions type="type:Text" override="true">
      <value>
        <![CDATA[
          Import the complete A03 data package into A04. Do not sync
          individual DocSets, Pages, or PageGroups. Do not read
          authoritativeSources on this task. Do not read BmlDocSetPlan.
          Do not edit A03. Do not write outside a04 data. Do not invent
          files that are not in A03 data.

          Source package: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data
          Source path:
          packages/bmldocs/blocks/org/blockml/bml/bmldocs/a03_authoring/data/

          Target package: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a04_rendering.data
          Target path:
          packages/bmldocs/blocks/org/blockml/bml/bmldocs/a04_rendering/data/

          Leave a04_rendering/task and A04_RenderingSector untouched.

          1. Delete live A04 data
          Delete the entire live A04 data tree (the target path above)
          including every descendant package (data.page, data.pagegroup,
          data.page.docs, and any other child). Delete every .bml file
          in that tree. Remove those A04 data Blocks from
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library. Do not remove A03 catalog
          entries, task entries, or other sectors.

          Ignore leftover non-package trees such as
          a04_rendering/data_IGNORE. They are not live A04 data. Do not
          read them, copy from them, or merge them. If they still hold
          old A04 files, do not treat those files as the current set.

          After this step A04 has no live data Blocks.

          2. Copy the full A03 data tree
          Copy every file and subdirectory from the A03 data path into
          the A04 data path, preserving relative paths. Example:
          a03_authoring/data/page/docs/Intro.bml
          → a04_rendering/data/page/docs/Intro.bml
          a03_authoring/data/pagegroup/RootPageGroup.bml
          → a04_rendering/data/pagegroup/RootPageGroup.bml
          a03_authoring/data/BmlDocSet_A03.bml
          → a04_rendering/data/BmlDocSet_A03.bml
          (the DocSet file name is remapped in step 3).

          Copy the complete tree once. Do not filter pages vs groups vs
          the DocSet. Do not skip a file because an older A04 copy
          existed. There is no older live A04 copy after step 1.

          3. Remap packages and names (one pass)
          After the copy, every imported file still names A03. Rewrite
          each imported file so it is an A04 Block. Apply these
          substitutions everywhere they appear — xmlns URIs, root
          element names, FQN comments, see-links, property values,
          TypeReference tokens, and prose that identifies this Block's
          sector:

          - package prefix
            org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data
            → org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a04_rendering.data
          - filesystem segment a03_authoring/data
            → a04_rendering/data (comments / examples only)
          - Block name BmlDocSet_A03 → BmlDocSet_A04
          - file BmlDocSet_A03.bml → BmlDocSet_A04.bml
            (rename the file; do not leave the A03 file name)
          - wording that says this Block is A03 / a03 / authoring
            data becomes A04 / a04 / rendering data

          Page and PageGroup Block names stay the same (Intro,
          RootPageGroup, …). Only the package and the DocSet name
          change.

          After the remap, an A04 file may reference only:
          - other A04 data Blocks (the remapped counterparts)
          - lib / docgen / core types (for example
            org.blockml.bml.documentation.*, org.blockml.bml.docgen.*)

          An A04 file must never reference a Block from another sector
          (a01_planning, a02_structuring, a03_authoring, or any later
          sector). Drop or remap such a reference. Do not keep an A03
          FQN because "the A04 counterpart is missing" — the counterpart
          is the remapped copy in this same import.

          Do not change A03 files. Do not change files outside the
          imported A04 data tree.

          4. Confirm the imported set
          The live A04 data package must contain the same relative
          files as A03 data, with packages and the DocSet name remapped.
          BmlDocSet_A04.pages, pageGroups, homePage, and rootPageGroup
          list only A04 Blocks. Each PageGroup parentGroup, pages, and
          landingPage list only A04 Blocks. See-links between imported
          Blocks point at A04 counterparts.

          5. Export imported A04 data from the catalog
          Export every Block under
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a04_rendering.data (including
          descendants) from org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library if it is
          not already in the catalog. Do not remove catalog entries of
          other sectors.
        ]]>
      </value>
    </instructions>
  </properties>
</task:A04_01_CopyData>
